    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Ok, I see both sides. But looking at the actual data from recent years, it seems like societies with very strong religious foundations tend to have much higher levels of trust and social capital compared to highly secularized ones. Doesn't that suggest that secularism might actually be more of a threat to long-term community cohesion than a solution for it?",
